   558	    # per message. Wrapping the runner puts a tick on every call boundary the
   559	    # run has — each sweep query, each `gws +read`, the `claude` call, and every
   560	    # CRM/bus write — so neither a 14-day backfill sweep nor one slow extraction
   561	    # can let a live run's lock go stale.
