    24	def _history_date(date_iso: Any) -> tuple[str, bool]:
    25	    """(YYYY-MM-DD, unparsed). gmail_source.normalise_date_iso is the ONE date
    26	    parser, so this re-runs it rather than trusting a raw `[:10]` slice: an
    27	    un-normalised RFC 2822 value reaching here used to become "Sun, 14 Se" and
    28	    land in a History entry looking like a real date. Anything it cannot read
    29	    falls back to today's UTC date AND reports itself, so the entry is dated
    30	    plausibly and says so instead of carrying a malformed date silently."""
    31	    normalised = normalise_date_iso(date_iso)
    32	    if normalised:
    33	        return normalised[:10], False
    34	    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).date().isoformat(), True
    35	
